title: Pensions and the Dole
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: social_welfare_timer = 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and social_welfare_timer = 0
card-image: img/portraits/John_Wheatley.jpg

= Pensions and the Dole



- @reduce_spending: Reduce unemployment benefits (the dole).
- @increase_spending_pre_depression: Increase unemployment benefits.
- @spending_same_pre_depression: Increase war pensions and disability benefits
- @spending_same_post_depression: Decrease war pensions and disability benefits
- @easy_discard
#- @cancel_advisor_action

@reduce_spending
subtitle: This will hurt our proletarian base. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; workers_labour -= 6; unemployed_labour -= 6; workers_cpgb += 3; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; dvp_relation += 5; tories_relation += 3; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; cpgb_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have reduced levels of social welfare spending. This means more poverty and suffering for the working class. Our detractors claim that we are sacrificing proletarian livelihoods for the sake of class peace with the bourgeoisie. 


@increase_spending_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_labour += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_labour += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

We have increased dole spending. Our proletarian base is pleased.

@spending_same_pre_depression
view-if: unemployed <= 15
choose-if: budget > 0
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: budget -= 1; workers_labour += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_labour += 6*(1-dissent); welfare += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if welfare > 1; welfare_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.3; unemployed -= 0.4; economic_growth += 0.2;

By spending more on war pensions and the disablity benefits we can help ease the burden on those still reeling from efects of the great war.


@spending_same_post_depression
subtitle: This will hurt our support with veterans. +1 Budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: welfare >= -5
on-arrival: budget += 1; workers_labour -= 6; unemployed_labour -= 6; workers_cpgb += 3; welfare -= 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; dvp_relation += 5; tories_relation += 3; pro_republic -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if in_grand_coalition and coalition_dissent > 0; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; cpgb_relation -= 8; inflation -= 0.3; unemployed += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2;

Cutting support for veterans is cruel. But I guess the budget needs to be balanced somehow...

[? if in_popular_front or in_left_front: The KPD is turning against us for our welfare policy. ?]
